## Required gates

- **Distribution terms:** G01 records owner-approved v2 source/binary terms,
  Academy redistribution permission and every framework-derived import's
  disposition under [distribution.md](distribution.md). No extraction before
  clearance; C26 verifies notices/terms against exact shipped inventory.

- **Provenance:** evaluate each direct import's actual license/notice and allowed
  usage. cdot-framework is not blanket MIT and its billing-retention condition
  cannot be erased by renaming. Prefer independently implemented patterns where
  direct copying is unsuitable. Academy sharing is owner-directed; establish
  package ownership and third-party notices rather than inventing a license.
- **Academy packaging:** React19/Tailwind4/Vite7 are observed in Academy, while
  the framework uses React18/Tailwind3. Select a compatible pinned desktop stack
  and one shared presentation source. The existing UI package re-exports app
  source and is not a ready independently reusable full learner app.
- **Shared-source changes:** propose the smallest extraction that supports actual
  web/desktop consumers. Keep Academy web behavior and hosted contracts stable;
  run both projects' affected tests. Pin the reviewed shared revision/package
  before completing its consuming desktop chunk.
- **SDK scan:** ec6230d2's accepted subset supplies synchronous scan. It requires
  explicit scan credentials; management OAuth is separate. Accepted Linux
  reports do not establish macOS ARM64 support. Qualify the native compiler/TLS
  dependencies, runtime integration, scanner contracts, cancellation, sanitized
  errors, and unknown outcomes in C02–C03.
- **SDK administration:** 32cbcb6d's accepted Phase4 is a candidate input for
  C08–C12. Map every actual operation, option, pagination bound, and error to
  accepted source/tests. SDK family labels are insufficient proof of parity.
- **SDK later families:** Phase5 Red Team/Model and Phase6 Gateway were developing
  or pending during inspection. Their exact accepted pins are prerequisites to
  C13/C16–C18. Do not consume unfinished work or substitute mocks as completion.
  Stable v2 must qualify the SDK subset it actually uses, including native/live
  evidence; it need not claim every unrelated SDK method is complete.
- **Harness:** retain the desktop-capable native engine/protocol after source and
  package checks. Do not substitute an older canonical checkout or npm launcher.
  Rebuild/reseal v2 resources to omit Node/managed CLI where proven unnecessary;
  old v1 resource hashes do not attest the changed v2 bundle. Preserve inference
  and MCP routing/context/tool restrictions.
# Behavioral and native test catalogue

These are required future tests and observable assertions, not results already
executed. G01/C01 bind them to exact commands. Each chunk names its applicable
IDs and adds feature-specific cases. Use fake transports/clocks/stores at real
module interfaces plus literal external fixtures; native and live tests provide
separate evidence. Do not assert implementation-private structure for its own sake.

## Core authority and SDK

- **T01 Context isolation:** tenant/workspace/credential switch during a request
  rejects old replies, retires pending reviews/one-time secrets, and cancels work.
  Switching back cannot revive authority. Credential replacement and sign-out
  behave the same way; duplicate completions settle at most once.
- **T02 Review authority:** forged/stale/replayed/consumed review IDs, changed
  draft/resource/context, model text, and imported history cannot Apply. Valid
  operator Apply transmits the exact reviewed operation once.
- **T03 Unknown outcomes:** disconnect before send, after send, timeout, cancel,
  401/403/429/5xx, and partial multistep provisioning yield correct states. No
  automatic mutation/scan replay; offer readback/review/explicit retry where valid.
- **T04 SDK external contract:** independently authored request/response fixtures
  verify method/path/body/headers/options, pagination/multipart limits, unknown
  enum/action preservation, sanitized errors, and no dropped options.
- **T05 Credential confinement:** scan-only setup works; management/inference/MCP
  credentials are separate. Deny wrong-origin redirects or custom endpoint
  changes that would forward a credential without an explicitly reviewed new
  destination binding. Preserve legitimate operator-reviewed endpoint overrides
  and explicitly selected nonsecret tenant-profile import; whitelist metadata,
  discard embedded secrets and never follow credential-file references.
  No implicit environment/tenant file
  loading, upstream fallback, persistent renderer storage, or secret log fields.
- **T06 Protected storage:** locked/denied/unavailable/corrupt store, interrupted
  write/reset, session-only mode, restart, explicit one-time reveal/clipboard,
  and cleanup. No plaintext fallback; v1 namespaces remain untouched.
- **T07 Lifecycle:** bounded concurrent work, cancellation, queue backpressure,
  superseding reads, app close/restart, sleep/wake, expired credentials, and
  monotonic versus wall-clock decisions. UI remains responsive during work.

## Presentation and Academy

- **T08 Shared presentation:** web and desktop consumers build from the same
  reviewed shared source; themes/fonts/routes render correctly. General desktop
  screens mount no Academy gamification/account effects or web manager routes.
- **T09 Native UI:** actual Tauri command path, menus/shortcuts, keyboard-only
  workflow, focus restoration, VoiceOver labels/order, zoom/large text, themes,
  reduced motion, long/empty/error content, and window resizing. Mock IPC tests
  alone cannot establish these. macOS WebDriver availability must be verified;
  use supported native accessibility/automation or recorded manual steps.
- **T10 Academy identity:** device grant, pending/slow_down/expiry/cancel, refresh,
  revocation, wrong issuer/client/scope, account switch/sign-out, and stale replies.
  Token management stays Rust-owned. The learner account is independent of tenant.
- **T11 Learning authority:** client bundles contain no answer keys/private lab
  evaluation, privileged routes, or assessor tokens. Forged verdict/award/local
  exam clock cannot pass; the hosted backend decides access, grading, and awards.
  Signed-in denial differs from guest sign-in; sandbox never uses tenant secrets.
- **T12 Offline work:** download lease/revision/account access, encrypted draft
  save/restart, locked vault, sign-out/account switch, withdrawn content, duplicate
  submission IDs, changed draft versions, and reconnection. No deferred action
  replay. Valid local work remains usable without claiming offline grading.

## Workflows and Harness

- **T13 Collection semantics:** exact capability subsets, large collections,
  bounded pagination/truncation, search/filter/page resets, stale/partial cache,
  consistent Home/Inbox source facts, and no false complete/zero/absent claims.
- **T14 API Client documents:** edit/save/conflict while typing, invalid input,
  environment/secret separation, import/path traversal/size errors, multipart,
  cookies/redirect auth, cancellation, history/download, Git/profile adoption,
  and recovery from interrupted writes. Arbitrary workbench targets cannot borrow
  privileged application credentials through renderer-supplied references.
- **T15 Harness process:** actual native binary and bounded bootstrap/JSONL
  protocol, malformed/oversized frames, correlation/duplicates, queue pressure,
  crash/EOF/cancel, context change, graceful/forced cleanup, and missing/tampered
  resources. No PATH launcher fallback or plaintext rollout/history.
- **T16 Harness authority:** typed investigation/proposal tools, active-draft
  protection, no engine Apply, one-time secrets absent from model context,
  read-only project defaults, approved single-process command restrictions,
  forbidden descendants/pipelines, stale decisions, and history replay.
- **T17 Inference/MCP identity:** pinned Gateway origin; SSO PKCE/state/nonce/
  issuer/client/audience/time/signature/JWKS/algorithm/key-rotation validation;
  sleep/refresh/revoke/identity changes;
  distinct inference/MCP grants; fixed conversation server scope; exact call-item
  approvals; changed revision/grant; denied tools; trace/execution evidence.
  No direct upstream provider fallback or global cross-workspace MCP authority.

## Import, quality, and artifacts

- **T18 Import transaction:** dry-run selection, versions/source lock, account
  match, protected source reads, malformed/oversized/traversal inputs, interruption
  at each commit point, restart, duplicate import, destination conflict, rollback,
  and source-byte preservation. No credentials/sessions/approvals transfer.
- **T19 Diagnostics privacy:** seeded canary secrets and customer content absent
  from logs/crash files/exports by default; explicit redacted export; correct
  retention/reset; no analytics/crash upload attempts; encrypted user history
  remains a distinct intentional storage feature.
- **T20 Performance:** named macOS hardware/OS/workloads, cold/warm startup, idle
  and scan/large-list/streaming/Harness memory, main-thread responsiveness, file
  and DMG footprint. Record methodology, repetitions, distribution and baseline;
  set core budgets in C03 and register later workload budgets at the introducing
  chunk's entry before implementation/acceptance measurement. See the budget
  governance below; C24/C26 compare with pre-registered values.
- **T21 Controlled live:** designated account/tenant/entitlements and disposable
  resources, explicit operation allowlist/budgets, sanitized request IDs, readback,
  cleanup receipts, deny/error cases, and unresolved outcome handling. Missing
  access or unsupported operations remain blocked; no destructive production tests.
- **T22 Installed package:** signed/notarized/stapled DMG, Gatekeeper/quarantine,
  mount/drag/install/launch/relaunch with fresh user/home and no developer checkout,
  PATH Node/Bun/managed CLI disabled, actual Rust sidecar, runtime inventory/hash
  integrity, no hidden backend download, safe uninstall/reset/coexistence,
  manual update, previous-version rollback, and preserved user work.
- **T23 Cross-feature offline:** launch offline and read/edit each applicable
  local category: saved cases, FP/FN reports, API Client documents, protected
  Harness history, configuration drafts, and Academy work. Mark remote data as
  stale/unknown as appropriate. Offline drafts do not retain valid Apply authority;
  reconnect requires fresh readback/review when needed. Pending reviews, scans,
  inference turns, generic HTTP mutations and MCP/tool calls never resubmit on
  reconnect. Offer explicit retry while preserving uncertain remote outcomes.
  Bind to C03,C09–C12,C14–C15,C17–C18,C20–C22 and cumulative C24.

## Performance budget governance
# Working-v1 parity and release closure

All v2 rows are **planned**. No v2 source/native/live/artifact result exists yet.
The baseline is [feature-baseline.md](feature-baseline.md); do not expand a
preview/stub into required live behavior without an explicit scope decision.

| Requirement family                     | Owning chunks   | Closure requirement                                                                  |
|----------------------------------------|-----------------|--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|
| Tenant setup/scan-only/protected state | C02,C03,C08,C23 | Context/capabilities, reviewed endpoint overrides/profile import, verification/reset |
| Runtime synchronous scan/cases         | C03,C12         | Faithful verdicts, profiles, cancellation and no silent replay                       |
| Profiles/topics/applications/keys      | C08,C09         | Exact supported reads/writes, review binding, one-time secrets                       |
| DLP/deployment catalogue               | C08,C10         | Exact supported operation subset and real multipart semantics                        |
| Sessions/content/search/cache          | C11             | Explicit reveal, protected persistence, bounded completeness                         |
| Metadata FP/FN reports                 | C11             | Edit/remove/undo/export without suppression side effects                             |
| Home/Inbox/source observations/charts  | C12,C18         | Runtime and Gateway data, freshness/partial/unknown/attention                        |
| Five-product Library/specifications    | C12             | Authoring/import/export; only supported Runtime execution                            |
| Red Team read-only observations        | C13             | Accepted actual reads; no invented live execution                                    |
| Model/skill read-only observations     | C13             | Accepted actual reads and partial-source disclosure                                  |
| API Client documents/projects/imports  | C14             | Fresh-input reconciliation, drafts/conflicts/secrets/Git adoption                    |
| API Client transport/history/catalogue | C15             | Real HTTP/cookies/downloads, scoped auth, no mutation bypass                         |
| Gateway workspace/config/admin subset  | C16,C17         | Supported scope/options and reviewed multi-step outcomes                             |
| Gateway inference/logs/telemetry/cost  | C18             | Streaming, route/model selection, operational budgets/limits                         |
| Harness native run/stream/lifecycle    | C19             | Real Rust engine/protocol, cleanup and no packaged Node runtime                      |
| Harness identity/protected history     | C20             | Rust SSO/key lifecycle, scope-safe restore/export/delete                             |
| Harness typed tools/project permission | C21             | Investigation/proposals and enforced existing sandbox restrictions                   |
| Workspace MCP                          | C22             | Rust auth/grants, exact call approvals and execution evidence                        |
| Academy identity/account isolation     | C04             | Device OAuth, scope admission, tenant-independent learner identity                   |
| Academy learner presentation           | C05             | Shared catalog/lessons/checks/sandbox/UI; feature-local gamification                 |
| Academy Program/exams/certificates     | C06             | Hosted access/timing/grading/award authority and account workflows                   |
| Academy encrypted offline work         | C07             | Lease/revision/account-aware reading/drafts; explicit submission                     |
| Reviewed imports/fresh authentication  | C23             | User work, source preservation, restart/rollback; no old approvals                   |
| Native UX/privacy/measured performance | C01–C24         | Per-chunk checks plus cumulative actual native quality closure                       |
| Controlled live behavior               | C25             | Designated scope, real outcomes, readback/cleanup, honest gaps                       |
| Signed installed package/update        | C26             | DMG/notary/Gatekeeper, exact bytes, fresh user, coexistence/rollback                 |

## Required per-workflow ledger

The [workflow ledger](../architecture/workflows.md) expands these families into
66 operation/workflow classes. C01 records machine-readable evidence rows and
consuming chunks map exact supported operations/options before implementation.
Every row needs an ID, baseline source, current classification, responsible chunk,
exact SDK/shared dependency contract, and independent expectations. Preserve four
evidence categories separately: source implementation, fixture/contract results,
native/live qualification, and final installed-artifact qualification. Record
denied/unsupported/partial results honestly rather than collapsing them to pass.

G01/C01 adds a live_requirement (required/not_required with reason) and separate
ready/blocked-by-access status to every row under [live-checks.md](live-checks.md).
The owner approves the expanded list before C25. Missing access cannot shrink
mandatory scope; a reduction requires a recorded owner decision and new review.
T23 cross-feature offline acceptance applies to local work and pending operations,
not just Academy. C24 closes that cumulative matrix.

V2 source completeness alone does not close a row. Each workflow needs applicable
success and failure assertions, context/authority coverage, native acceptance and
required live/artifact evidence. C25/C26 review the cumulative ledger against
the final frozen input set. A required blocked check blocks stable completion.

## Intentional non-goals and retained classifications

- Financial desktop billing/monetization and media-generation infrastructure are
  excluded. Remote operational cost/limit administration is retained.
- Exception Patterns remains explicitly synthetic/inert if shown. FP/FN reports
  do not suppress scans or modify policy.
- New Red Team execution and dedicated Model Security execution remain outside
  parity. Their existence in the new SDK does not authorize adding product scope.
- Academy admin/assessor operations remain web-only. Learner feedback with an
  administrative namespace is classified by actual authority, not string matching.
- No browser app, in-app updater, or additional supported OS/architecture is
  required for first stable v2.

